00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
This week: Iran war risk, Hormuz pressure, Shangri-La, and Taiwan's AI supply chain.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.500
"The naval blockade that, until now, we have been patient about"

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:15.000
"and have not attacked you over -- we will break that naval blockade."

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
"But more importantly, let me tell you:"

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.000
"has not been very significant."

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.000
"the impact has been relatively limited."

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.000
"However, prices in the markets have increased by around 3%."

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
"At present, about 9,700 of our containers are being held."

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:46.000
"Top defense officials from around the world meet in Singapore for the annual Shangri-La Dialogue."

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:55.000
"The summit, held by the London-based International Institute for Strategic Studies, is a space for major powers to have conversations and issue warnings."

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:05.000
"In a keynote speech, Vietnamese President To Lam called for the enforcement of international law to confront global challenges."

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:14.000
To Lam: "We recognize competition as inevitable, but it must be within the bounds of the law, transparency, and self-restraint."

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:23.000
"Today's global crisis is not an inevitable consequence that we are forced to accept."

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:31.000
Hegseth: "Well thank you all very much for being here. Thank you for your patience."

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:39.000
"It's been a long couple of days but productive couple of days."

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.000
"America's a global superpower with global obligations."

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:51.000
"The 2026 Shangri-La Dialogue has concluded in Singapore after three days of discussions focused on the world's security challenges."

00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:00.000
"Defense officials and military leaders from across the globe gathered amid growing concerns over conflicts in the Middle East and rising tensions in the Indo-Pacific."

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:09.000
"Much of the forum centered on China's military expansion and its impact on regional security."

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:18.000
"On Day 2, US defense secretary Pete Hegseth delivered a keynote speech calling on allies to boost defense spending in the face of China's expansive military buildup."

